  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Nor'easter filling as it sits along the NJ coast.\n\nThe nor-easter center is just off NJ and will circulate back to\nthe shoreline before sliding to the east and north later \ntonight and Monday. It is already starting to fill and will do\nso very slowly today and as it moves away. The wind and gusts\nwill start to decrease a bit through the daylight hours, and\nwill do so even more tonight. The loosening pressure gradient\nwill mean that the threat for nearing wind advisory criteria\nover any of our counties is all but over. We did knock a couple\ndegs off the dewpoints for today as the NBM has been\nconsistently too high over the past 2-3 days. Despite this, the\nbands of rain should go farther to the west than Sat - so we\nbumped the PoPs to categorical for most of the CWA east of route\n219. The rain may not quite reach the ground in the western\nlayer of zones, but some hit the ground locally despite the\nlower-than-forecast dewpoints on Sat. Cool air is locked in, and\nmaxes will be only 55-65F - coolest NE.\n\nQPF is looking heaviest just about where it was on Saturday -\nthe Lower Susq. Someone might pick up another inch, but most\nlikely not. Even so, the FFG is high enough to not have flooding\neven be a thought. \n\nConditions will improve tonight and Monday morning. By noon\nMonday, there should only be isolated --SHRA over the NE and the\nwind will not be notable. Temps rise slightly from Sun, but will\nstill be cooler than normal. \n\n  -----------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Tranquil conditions expected for the first half \nof next week with a slight warming trend emerging across the \nregion.\n\nDry conditions will continue into Thursday as the front\nanticipated to be arriving late Wed/night will be delayed for a\nday or so. It will pick up some moisture from the remnants of\nPolo. But, that precip probably stays to our W until Thursday. All\nmodel guidance trends towards a warming trend in this \ntimeframe, with above-average temperatures prevailing area wide\nfor the balance of the week. Someone may hit 80F before Friday.\nDetails on timing and intensity of rainfall are not easy to pin\ndown at this range and with the upcoming pattern. So, we'll just\nmake a gradual increase in PoPs Fri-Sat-Sun.",
